  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Corlanor Criteria Version 2; Original: 9/17/19; Approval: 11/15/2019; Update: 04/19/2024; Effective: 06/1/2024.",
    "Closed adult HF, pediatric DCM and IST pathways use indication when gates. Clinical thresholds, ages, prior therapy alternatives and the functioning demand pacemaker exception use attestations; supporting documentation requires manual review. No age restriction is imposed on the IST pathway.",
    "Cautions (notes only): females should use effective contraception due to fetal toxicity; monitor for atrial fibrillation; not recommended in patients with second degree AV block; monitor heart rate throughout therapy. Manual review required.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months. Manual review required.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): 60 – 5mg tablets; 60 – 7.5mg tablets; 450ml – 5mg/5ml oral solution. Source does not specify a quantity time period. Quantity enforcement requires manual review."
  ],
